# King ring, distinct fraction.
# BKS = **matched quench rate 2e13, 3 independent seeds** (90210/90211/90212).
#   -> BKSsd is the MEASURED run-to-run scatter (not an estimate from mixed rates).
# err = Poisson(7net) (+) measured BKS sd.  NOT double-counted:
#   the 3-seed sd already contains counting noise, so no Poisson is added on the BKS side.
#   7net has 1 seed -> only counting error; its true uncertainty is LARGER than shown.
# p = two-sided t-test, 2 dof, prediction interval sd*sqrt(1+1/3). **Prefer p over sigma**
#   -- with n=3 the sd itself is uncertain, so 'N sigma' reads as overconfident.
# other rates (5e12, 5e13, 5e12*) are plotted as dots, not in the bar. See NOTE 'S4 analysis 19'.
#   n    7net%  BKSmean%   BKSsd%  otherLo%  otherHi%   diff%p   err%p  sigma       p
